## #01 — Notes and contract
Read pins and 06.01. Write notes FIRST in new 06.02.md. Preserve source-before
bytes and record every changed furniture section's why and this #NN authorization.
Write an explicit return-capture/1 contract in the new lab README, with examples.
Reserve -> complete local capture -> Git publication. Prime review binds to that
exact package and may occur locally before publication or against its published
bytes. Publication never implies review or acceptance.
A local completion receipt says only that capture finished and hashes verified.
It does not approve, accept, seat, publish or finish the underlying work.

## #02 — One return member per submitted revision
Use this book's existing 0100–0199 band; members start at 0101. No extra axis,
top-level return queue, new desk or silent band extension. If full, stop.
Implement reserve, capture and verify in labs/return-capture-pass01/return_capture.py
with Python standard library. The lab has README/tests/evidence. No app dispatch.
Reserve uses the lowest free member and exclusive directory creation. All existing
page folders/drafts count as taken; retries cannot allocate an occupied number.
The same submission reservation returns the existing reservation or a conflict;
concurrent calls cannot reserve two members for the same submission identity.
Prime reserves the explicit destination before a future pack is released; its
builder submits only there. Future templates include originating book/page/05.NN,
expected outputs, submitter/reviewer labels and the exact reserved destination.
Labels and recorded release text grant no authority. The helper chooses no route.

Return member shape (one page number/name):
- 01.md: generated index/identity and links; it directs readers to verify the
  completion receipt rather than storing a second editable completion status;
- reservation.json: originating batch, submission id, allocated path and labels;
- return.md: the exact independently supplied Builder return bytes;
- manifest.json: source/baseline identities, return hash, selected payload hashes,
  byte lengths, logical source/destination mapping, required/omitted evidence;
- payload/0001.blob etc: exact code/tests/docs/evidence bytes selected by an explicit
  input manifest. No recursive repo copy or filename-based execution;
- receipt.json: local capture completion marker, written last, binding manifest
  and reservation hashes. Completion is derived by verification, not 01.md prose.
No self-referential manifest hash. No ZIP required; a ZIP may later be a derived
transport copy with its own checksum, not the only record.

Capture input is a dedicated return file plus an explicit list of artifacts and
relative logical names under a declared source root. Snapshot required inputs
and dependencies or pin them at a retained baseline with explicit hashes; report
missing evidence. Never parse the first Review heading to extract return bytes.
Do not invent an unavailable historic file, original submission timestamp or test.
Code files are archived data; the capture tool never executes them.
Capture copies bytes to the reserved local page, verifies the copy and source
identities, then writes receipt last. No overwrite/truncation of captured files.
Re-submit same submission id and identical bytes -> already-captured/no writes.
Same identity with changed bytes -> conflict; amended submission needs a new
member and supersedes link. Partial packages remain visible and cannot silently
be completed/replaced by a retry. Report retained paths for explicit recovery.
Concurrency/exclusive writes must not produce two clean claims for one slot or
clean receipts over mixed payloads. No same-user malicious-write confinement claim.
Reject path escapes, invalid aliases, symlinks/junctions or hard-link output tricks;
all reads/writes stay in declared roots. New file writes are exclusive.

