## #04 — Meaningful isolated tests
Use disposable books; no real return member allocation during the build.
Cover lowest-free and occupied/temp slots; two concurrent reservations; full band;
clean capture/fresh-process verify; identical retry/no writes; changed return or
payload conflict; required file missing; bytes changed during copy; injected
interruption before receipt; partial receipt; corrupt manifest/receipt; malformed
types and duplicate keys; traversal/link aliases; CRLF-vs-LF exactness. Retain test
failures and explain privilege skips. No real stores, model calls or networking.
Demonstrate local capture without a .git directory or network, then publish a copy
in a disposable local Git repo and verify every captured blob at its actual
commit. Publication is separate evidence and cannot mutate the sealed package.
Snapshot all source/target names/bytes around refused/idempotent operations.

