No shared Git writes. Prime verifies, performs the first real local captures,
then commits/pushes those exact bytes and verifies stored blobs/remote commit.
If Git publication fails, local complete packages remain complete and unpublished;
do not rebuild, change ids, or call them accepted to retry a push. Record actual
publication commit in a separate acknowledgement/review after verification; do
not rewrite receipt.json to add a circular self-commit reference.
Allowed writes: new lab, this page's notes/return/evidence and the three specified
furniture files. No active builder pages/code, app/, Clerk store, Prime-support,
SoF, original root packs/returns, kernel or protected source checkouts.
Builder report is not release, approval, review or activation.

